-- title:
--   Perfect antisymmetric pairing on a non-Eisenstein corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain and $k$ a field which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra such that $\mathcal{O} \to k$ is surjective. Let $M' \ge 1$, let $H' \le (\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$ be a subgroup, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals. Write $\mathrm{H}^1 = \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(M')^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal{O})$ for the additive homomorphisms from the group $\Gamma_{H'}(M') \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (the image in $\Gamma_0(M')$ of the preimage of $H'$ under the determinant-type character `gamma0Units`) to $\mathcal{O}$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra acting on $\mathrm{H}^1$ compatibly with the $\mathcal{O}$-action, the action being faithful (any $t$ killing all of $\mathrm{H}^1$ is $0$). Let $\mathrm{Gen}$ be the type with constructors $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M'$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid M'$) and $\langle d \rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$), and let $\mathrm{op} : \mathrm{Gen} \to \mathbb{T}$ be such that each $\mathrm{op}(g)$ acts on $\mathrm{H}^1$ as [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) does, i.e. by the corestriction-of-conjugation operator `heckeTL` at $\ell$ resp. $q$ for $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and by `diamondL` for $\langle d \rangle$; assume the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the image of $\mathrm{op}$ is all of $\mathbb{T}$. Let $\theta\!\!-\!\!\mathrm{bar} : \mathrm{Gen} \to k$ be a function. Let $S'$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb{T}$: a complete family of orthogonal idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb{T}$ and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j \iff i \neq j$. Fix $i_0$, and let $\pi_k$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb{T}e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0}) = \theta\!\!-\!\!\mathrm{bar}(g)$ for every generator $g$. Assume the non-Eisenstein condition: some prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M'$ and $\ell \equiv 1 \bmod M'$ has $\theta\!\!-\!\!\mathrm{bar}(T_\ell) \neq \ell + 1$ in $k$. Then, writing $P$ for the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot \mathrm{H}^1$, there is an $\mathcal{O}$-bilinear form $\beta : P \to P \to \mathcal{O}$ such that $v \mapsto \beta(v,\cdot)$ is a bijection onto $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal{O}}(P,\mathcal{O})$, $\beta(v,w) = -\beta(w,v)$, and $\beta(av,w) = \beta(v,aw)$ for all $a$ in the corner ring.
--
--   This is the self-duality of a non-Eisenstein local factor of weight-two cohomology: the restriction to the corner of the cup-product pairing twisted by the Fricke involution, perfect and alternating by Poincaré duality on the modular curve and perfect after base change because $\mathcal{O}$ is torsion-free, with the Hecke action self-adjoint. It is used in the construction of the Galois action on the ordinary line of the corner module modulo $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_exists_perfectPairing_antisymm_cornerSubmodule_H1_of_not_isEisenstein.lean

